# Hustronix product stack

## Architecture

- **Backend**: Node + Express + WebSocket in repo root [`src/server.ts`](src/server.ts), SQLite via [`src/database.ts`](src/database.ts). Default HTTP port **3005** (`PORT`).
- **Frontend**: Next.js App Router in [`hustronix-ui/`](hustronix-ui/). Default dev port **3000**. Production = two processes (API + `next start`) unless reverse-proxied to one origin.

## Environment

**API (root `.env`):** `PORT`, `ALLOWED_ORIGINS` (comma-separated; must include the Next origin, e.g. `http://localhost:3000`), `MISSION_CONTROL_API_KEY`, LLM keys as needed.

**UI (`hustronix-ui/.env.local`):**

- **`NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL`** — Absolute API origin (e.g. `http://127.0.0.1:3005`) **or leave unset / empty** so browser calls same-origin `/api/*` (recommended with cookies).
- **`API_PROXY_TARGET`** (server-only, Next rewrites) — Where Next proxies `/api/:path*` when using same-origin mode; default `http://127.0.0.1:3005`.
- **`NEXT_PUBLIC_WS_URL`** — Chat WebSocket (e.g. `ws://127.0.0.1:3005`). On localhost, [`api.ts`](hustronix-ui/src/lib/api.ts) can fall back to port 3005 when HTTP base is empty.
- Optional **`NEXT_PUBLIC_API_KEY`** if not sending `x-user-id` / cookie session.

## Auth contract

- REST [`authMiddleware`](src/middleware/auth.ts): **`Bearer hx_live_…`** user tokens → cookie **`hustronix_session`** (opaque DB session) → legacy **`hustronix_uid`** → **`x-api-key` + `x-user-id`** (automation) → **`x-user-id`** on loopback only → **`system`** for local/key-only.
- Passwords: **bcrypt** (12 rounds); legacy SHA-256 verifies once then upgrades. Rate limits on **`/api/auth/register`**, **`/api/auth/login`**, **`/api/auth/password`** ([`rateLimit.ts`](src/middleware/rateLimit.ts)).
- **`POST /api/auth/logout`** revokes the session matching the cookie. Sessions + API keys: **`GET/POST/DELETE /api/auth/api-keys`**, **`GET/DELETE /api/auth/sessions`**, **`POST /api/auth/sessions/revoke-all`**. Profile updates: **`PATCH /api/me`** → `settings` keys **`profile.*`**.
- **`external_signals.user_id`** scopes signals (migration default **`system`**); **`system`** principal sees all tenant signals.
- WebSocket: session cookie / **`?session=`** / loopback **`?userId=`**; production rejects remote anonymous sockets ([`resolveWsUserId`](src/middleware/auth.ts)).
- UI **`credentials: "include"`** ([`api.ts`](hustronix-ui/src/lib/api.ts)); localStorage **`hustronix_userId`** is dev convenience for loopback **`x-user-id`**.

**Proxy note:** Same-origin `/api` rewrites help cookies; if `Set-Cookie` is dropped by a proxy, align cookie `Domain`/`Path` or terminate auth at the edge.

## Wired UI routes (live API)

| Route | Behavior |
|-------|----------|
| `/mission-control` | `GET /api/mission-control/summary`, `GET /api/decisions`, `POST /api/decisions/commit`, WebSocket `COMMIT_DECISION` |
| `/execute` | `GET /api/execution/ledger?scope=all`, `GET /api/execution/capacity`, `POST /api/execution/transition` |
| `/signals` | `GET /api/execution/signals/by-state`, `POST /api/execution/link` |
| `/chat` | WebSocket: `text`, `text_chunk`, `history`, `new_session` |
| `/reports` | `GET /api/metrics/reports` |
| `/teams` | `GET /api/metrics/teams` |
| `/profile` | `GET/PATCH /api/me`, `GET /api/activity`, `GET/POST/DELETE /api/auth/api-keys`, sessions endpoints |
| `/settings` | `GET /api/settings`, `POST /api/settings/bulk` (General + Notifications toggles mapped to `PREF.*`) |

## Still mock / partial

- Profile **Security** password form UI (backend **`POST /api/auth/password`** exists).
- Settings **Organization** free-text and some tabs (Rules/Capacity in UI only).
- **Live ingestion** into `external_signals` is via API/UI/seeding only (Telegram/Slack bridges removed from this repo).

## Implementation rules

1. **New UI data** — Prefer `apiGet`/`apiPost` from [`hustronix-ui/src/lib/api.ts`](hustronix-ui/src/lib/api.ts); map DB shapes in [`mappers.ts`](hustronix-ui/src/lib/mappers.ts).
2. **New API** — Use `authMiddleware`; scope by `(req as any).userId`; keep responses JSON-stable for the UI.
3. **CORS** — Add every browser origin that hosts the UI to `ALLOWED_ORIGINS`; use `credentials: true` + explicit origins when cookies matter.
4. **Product positioning** — Ledger + auditor = source of truth; LLM/chat is an interface into that system, not a replacement for enforcement rules.
